  <div class="pl-cards">
    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>common/di/AppScopeModule.kt — new @ApplicationScope qualifier + Hilt provider</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p>Declares the <code>@ApplicationScope</code> qualifier annotation and a <code>@Singleton</code> Hilt provider in <code>SingletonComponent</code>. Reuses the already-provided <code>@Dispatcher(TrailsDispatchers.IO)</code> dispatcher — no new dispatcher needed.</p>
        <!-- @include diff-block { "lines": [
          { "kind": "add", "text": "@Qualifier @Retention(AnnotationRetention.RUNTIME) annotation class ApplicationScope" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "@Module @InstallIn(SingletonComponent::class) object AppScopeModule {" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "  @Provides @Singleton @ApplicationScope" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "  fun provideApplicationScope(@Dispatcher(TrailsDispatchers.IO) io: CoroutineDispatcher): CoroutineScope" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "    = CoroutineScope(SupervisorJob() + io)" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "}" }
        ] } -->
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>data/ArticleRepository.kt — replace bare scope initialiser with @ApplicationScope injection</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p>Removes <code>ioDispatcher</code> from the constructor (no remaining usage after removal) and the bare <code>CoroutineScope(ioDispatcher)</code> field. Adds <code>@ApplicationScope coroutineScope: CoroutineScope</code>. The four launch/async sites (<code>add</code>, <code>delete</code>, <code>synchronize</code>, <code>searchHybrid</code>) already use the name <code>coroutineScope</code> — no body edits needed.</p>
        <!-- @include diff-block { "lines": [
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "@Dispatcher(TrailsDispatchers.IO) private val ioDispatcher: CoroutineDispatcher" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "@ApplicationScope private val coroutineScope: CoroutineScope" },
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "private val coroutineScope = CoroutineScope(ioDispatcher)" }
        ] } -->
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>services/firestore/FirestoreSyncManager.kt — inject shared scope, neuter cleanup()</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p>Removes the ad-hoc <code>CoroutineScope(SupervisorJob() + Dispatchers.IO)</code> field. Adds <code>@ApplicationScope scope: CoroutineScope</code> to the constructor. <strong>Critical:</strong> <code>cleanup()</code> replaces <code>scope.cancel()</code> with a comment — the singleton scope must never be cancelled by a single consumer.</p>
        <!-- @include diff-block { "lines": [
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "private val scope = CoroutineScope(SupervisorJob() + Dispatchers.IO)" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "// @ApplicationScope CoroutineScope injected — app-lifetime managed, do not cancel" },
          { "kind": "ctx", "text": "fun cleanup() { cancelPeriodicSync() /* scope.cancel() removed — shared singleton */ }" }
        ] } -->
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>test/…/common/di/AppScopeIsolationTest.kt — supervised-isolation unit test</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p>Pure kotlinx-coroutines-test unit test. Builds <code>CoroutineScope(SupervisorJob() + StandardTestDispatcher(testScheduler))</code>; launches a throwing child; asserts <code>scope.isActive == true</code>; launches a sibling and asserts it completes normally. No Firebase, no WorkManager, no MockK. Gradle task: <code>./gradlew :app:testDebugUnitTest</code>.</p>
        <!-- @include diff-block { "lines": [
          { "kind": "add", "text": "val scope = CoroutineScope(SupervisorJob() + StandardTestDispatcher(testScheduler))" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "scope.launch { throw IllegalStateException(\"child failure\") }" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "advanceUntilIdle()" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "assertTrue(scope.isActive) // SupervisorJob absorbs child failure" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "scope.launch { counter++ }; advanceUntilIdle(); assertEquals(1, counter)" }
        ] } -->
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>

  <!-- @include callout { "kind": "risk", "title": "HIGH — cleanup() must NOT cancel the shared singleton scope", "body": "<code>FirestoreSyncManager.cleanup()</code> calls <code>scope.cancel()</code>. After consolidation the scope is <code>@Singleton</code>; cancelling it kills all future coroutines in ArticleRepository and any future consumer for the process lifetime. Replace with a no-op comment." } -->
